Atlas overlay patch 0061: security/keyring-label
Why: the key that encrypts cookies and saved passwords is kept in the login keyring under a name the
engine hard-codes ("Chromium Safe Storage", application "chromium"). The person sees that name in the
keyring manager and in `secret-tool`, and any other browser built from the same engine would share the
key. The entry is now "Atlas Safe Storage", application "atlas", so it is ours, readable and not
shared. A lower tier (flag, policy, pref) does not exist for this name; three constants, no logic.
A profile moved from the previous browser package keeps its files but not its old key: the sites
it was signed in to ask once more (recorded in the atlas-keyring journey).
Files: components/os_crypt/async/browser/freedesktop_secret_key_provider.h
Test filter: FreedesktopSecretKeyProviderTest.*; journey atlas-keyring (secret-tool search shows the Atlas entry)
Rebase risk: L (three constants in a header; the Chrome-branded block above is untouched)
Release: 0.13
License: BSD-3-Clause (hunk in an engine file the inherited series does not touch)
Verified at: 156.0.8078.79, prepared tree with the inherited and platform series applied

